ina, cement clinker, dolomite, and limestone; and terminal and stevedoring services. The company also provides cargo loading, cargo discharge, port and terminal operations, vessel chartering, voyage planning, and technical vessel management. It owns and operates a fleet of 7 vessels. The company was founded in 1996 and is headquartered in Newport, Rhode Island.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Mads Rosenberg Boye Petersen | President, CEO & Director | Age 45 | Compensation: $822,125 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 170 people. Revenue per employee of $3.7M ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $291K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $24K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Pangaea Logistics Solutions Ltd is a small-cap industrials business with a $608M market cap on $632M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -3% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 21% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 12-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $49M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.77\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 1.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 51% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.2375366568914946},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 60% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 53% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance she